# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually copies.
#
# target/ is ~9k files and 1.6GB on a checkout that has been built
# locally, against 24 files of everything else. BuildKit walks the whole
# context before it copies anything, so leaving it in costs every local
# build and buys nothing — the Dockerfile only takes Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock and src/.
#
# This used to be covered by onym-infra's rsync excludes, which no
# longer apply now that deploys build these contexts directly rather
# than on the droplet (onymchat/onym-infra#13).
.git/
target/

# The Dockerfile copies none of these, so nothing is baked into a layer
# today. They are excluded anyway: a build context is the wrong place
# for a DeviceCheck key to be sitting when someone later reaches for
# `COPY . .`.
secrets/
*.p8
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
*.log
